# Grids

Use [Material grids](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/reference/grids/) to lay out equal cards or blocks on a page. This is the documentation layout, not the PDFormy `grid` block. `attr_list` and `md_in_html` are enabled.

A card grid is a list inside a `div` with the classes `grid` and `cards`. The `markdown` attribute is required. Leave a blank line after the opening tag and before the closing tag.

```html
<div class="grid cards" markdown>

-   __Table__

    ---

    A header row and typed columns.

    [Table](tables/index.md)

</div>
```

- One card is one list item. The bold line is the title, `---` separates the body, and the last line is the link.
- A generic grid uses `<div class="grid" markdown>` and holds blocks such as admonitions or code fences. Add `{ .card }` on its own line under a block to give that block a card.
- Cards wrap to full width when the page is narrow. Do not set a column count.
- A content tab can sit in a generic grid. The tab syntax is in the content tabs rule.
